<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  A small synthetic MuseumPlus RIA dump, for the tests and for trying the ingest.

  **It is shaped like the real export, not like a convenient fixture.** It
  carries the fields the shipped mapping actually reads: ObjObjectTitleVrt,
  ObjObjectNumberTxt, ObjTechnicalTermClb, ObjMaterialTechniqueVrt, ObjDateVrt,
  ObjPerAssociationMainParticipantNameVrt, ObjOwnerRef, the ObjOrgGroupVoc /
  MaterialVoc / ObjCategoryVoc references, and the ObjObjectTitleGrp title list
  (SortLnu + TitleTxt).

  An earlier version of this file carried `ObjObjectTitleClb` — which the real
  export *never* has — and lacked `ObjObjectTitleVrt`, which every real object
  does have. Fixture-based tests therefore could not see a title, and dc:title
  was left out of the mapping for the Object module as a result. **Keep this
  file representative**: the values below are invented, the shape is not.

  Also like the real dump:
    * `moduleItem` carries only `hasAttachments` and `id` — no `uuid` (uuid is
      broken in the instance we mirror, so @id is the key);
    * `virtualField` has a bare `<value>`, no dataType and no formattedValue;
    * every object has a title, an owner reference and a `__lastModified`.

  The three `__lastModified` values are load-bearing: a test rewrites two of
  them to give all three records the same datestamp, to exercise the keyset
  cursor against a non-unique key.
-->
